{"title":"Career Roadmap — Wildlife Researcher","role":"Wildlife Researcher","summary":"A Wildlife Researcher studies wild animals, their behavior, ecology, populations, habitats, conservation status, and interactions with ecosystems. The role combines zoology, ecology, field biology, statistics, GIS, conservation science, and research methodology.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science - General / Honours)","Course":"Zoology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Wildlife Researcher studies wild animals, their behavior, ecology, populations, habitats, conservation status, and interactions with ecosystems. The role combines zoology, ecology, field biology, statistics, GIS, conservation science, and research methodology."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wildlife surveys"},{"text":"Animal behavior studies"},{"text":"Population monitoring"},{"text":"Habitat assessment"},{"text":"Biodiversity surveys"},{"text":"Camera-trap studies"},{"text":"Conservation research"},{"text":"Human-wildlife conflict studies"},{"text":"Ecological data analysis"},{"text":"Scientific publications"},{"text":"Conservation planning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Zoology graduate, a Master's degree is strongly recommended for a long-term research career, especially for independent research, specialist, scientist, and academic positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc Zoology"},{"text":"Zoology + ecology + field research + statistics"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Research Intern / Field Research Assistant"},{"text":"Wildlife surveys + data collection"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Wildlife Researcher / Project Associate"},{"text":"Species and ecosystem research"}],[{"text":"2037–2041"},{"text":"Senior Researcher / Conservation Scientist"},{"text":"Advanced research + project leadership"}],[{"text":"2041–2046"},{"text":"Principal Researcher / Research Lead"},{"text":"Research programs + conservation strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Sc","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Zoological Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Animal diversity"},{"text":"Animal anatomy"},{"text":"Animal physiology"},{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Evolution"},{"text":"Basic ecology"},{"text":"Biodiversity"},{"text":"Scientific observation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic field skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Species observation"},{"text":"Field-note recording"},{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Identification"},{"text":"GPS basics"},{"text":"Scientific documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Ecology & Wildlife Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Animal behavior"},{"text":"Population ecology"},{"text":"Community ecology"},{"text":"Evolutionary biology"},{"text":"Biogeography"},{"text":"Conservation biology"},{"text":"Environmental science"},{"text":"Taxonomy"},{"text":"Wildlife management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Begin learning:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Wildlife survey methods"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Research Specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wildlife ecology"},{"text":"Conservation genetics"},{"text":"Population monitoring"},{"text":"Behavioral ecology"},{"text":"Biodiversity assessment"},{"text":"Field research methodology"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Scientific writing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The final-year project should ideally involve real field observations or a structured wildlife/ecological dataset."}]},{"heading":"Core Wildlife Science Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"