nd protected-area permissions when conducting fieldwork."}]},{"heading":"Wildlife Data Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern wildlife researcher should be comfortable with quantitative analysis."},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Generalized linear models"},{"text":"Multivariate analysis"},{"text":"Survival analysis"},{"text":"Population estimation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Ecological Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Eventually learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Occupancy modelling"},{"text":"Species distribution modelling"},{"text":"Mark-recapture analysis"},{"text":"Distance sampling"},{"text":"Biodiversity indices"},{"text":"Population viability analysis"},{"text":"Spatial statistics"}]}]},{"heading":"GIS & Remote Sensing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"GIS is one of the highest-value technical skills for wildlife research."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"ArcGIS"},{"text":"Google Earth Engine"},{"text":"GPS/GNSS"},{"text":"Spatial databases"},{"text":"Raster/vector data"},{"text":"Land-use mapping"},{"text":"Habitat mapping"},{"text":"Landscape analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Remote Sensing"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Satellite imagery"},{"text":"NDVI"},{"text":"Land-cover classification"},{"text":"Habitat fragmentation"},{"text":"Vegetation monitoring"},{"text":"Change detection"},{"text":"Drone imagery fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Zoology","Wildlife Ecology","GIS","Statistics"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Programming & Research Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"R — Advanced Priority"},{"type":"p","text":"R is especially v